hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15837","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, said: I do not see the blood money except for the paternal relatives, for they pay it on his behalf; has any of you heard anything from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about that? Al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi said, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had employed him over the Bedouins: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wrote to me to give the wife of Ashyam al-Dababi a share of her husband's blood money, so Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah Almighty be pleased with him, acted upon that."
"15838","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard it from al-Zuhri, from Said, that Umar said: The blood money belongs to the paternal relatives, and the wife does not inherit from her husband's blood money, until al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wrote to him to give the wife of Ashyam al-Dababi a share of her husband's blood money, so Umar retracted his saying."
"15839","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Judan, from al-Hasan, from al-Dahhak ibn Sufyan al-Kilabi, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: O Dahhak, what is your food? He said: O Messenger of Allah, meat and milk. He said: Then what does it become? He said: Into what you know. He said: For Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has made what comes out of the son of Adam an example of this world."
